WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.539
Miles stood outside the special palace entrance that was used for guards and the king's swordsmen. When

2
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.449
he spotted a guard, he hurried over to the doorway. "Can you take a message to Sir

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.195
Humphrey Marlow, please?" he asked. "Sir Humphrey died five years ago," said the guard, eyeing Miles suspiciously.

4
00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:23.197
"But I'll fetch his son." Miles waited nervously until the guard returned at last with a young boy.

5
00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:28.523
"I am Sir Humphrey's son, also named Humphrey," the boy told him. "I am the king's whipping

6
00:00:28.524 --> 00:00:36.444
boy too." The boy suddenly looked at him intently. "Are you Miles Hendon?" Startled, Miles didn't answer,

7
00:00:36.445 --> 00:00:42.005
but the boy said, "I believe you are. The king described you to me. Please follow me."

8
00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:51.420
Miles was stunned. Why would the young king know about him? Was he about to be arrested?

9
00:00:51.421 --> 00:00:57.499
As they passed by the kitchen, Miles noticed that the cooks and servants had gathered together and

10
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:05.990
were whispering in hushed tones. "Has something happened?" asked Miles. "You shall soon find out," Humphrey said.

11
00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:08.975
They turned down a long corridor that led to the great hall of the palace. By now

12
00:01:08.976 --> 00:01:16.897
the celebration following the coronation had begun. The hall was filled with lords and ladies in their finery.

13
00:01:16.898 --> 00:01:25.151
At the far end, on a splendid throne, sat a boy wearing the jeweled crown of England.

14
00:01:25.152 --> 00:01:31.977
Miles blinked in surprise. "Is this a dream? Could that be . . . Is that my

15
00:01:31.978 --> 00:01:39.703
young friend?" He stepped closer to see better. "For certain, it is he!" Without thinking, Miles rushed

16
00:01:39.704 --> 00:01:44.783
toward Edward. Edward looked up in surprise. "Miles!" he cried. Another person gasped. "Miles!" It was Hugh

17
00:01:44.784 --> 00:01:48.463
Hendon, whose face had gone white at the sight of his brother. For now Miles was mesmerized

18
00:01:48.464 --> 00:01:53.119
by the sight in front of him—the boy on the throne. He was utterly bewildered until he

19
00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:01.119
realized the truth: The boy had not been lying after all! He really was the king of

20
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:07.523
England! "Your Majesty." Miles dropped to his knees and bowed his head. He felt so ashamed for having

21
00:02:07.524 --> 00:02:17.438
doubted Edward all this time. "I'm so glad you found your way to me," murmured Edward, placing

22
00:02:17.439 --> 00:02:22.691
his hand on Miles' shoulder. The two friends looked at each other with affection. "I promised to

23
00:02:22.692 --> 00:02:26.922
always look after you, didn't I, Your Majesty?" said Miles. "You always keep your promises. And so

24
00:02:26.923 --> 00:02:35.917
do I," Edward replied. Then he said to the assembled crowd, "May I present to you my

25
00:02:35.918 --> 00:02:41.082
trusty and well-beloved servant—Miles Hendon, the man who saved my life more than once. He not only

26
00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:46.740
protected your king; he believed in him, gave him courage, and became his friend. Miles Hendon, Earl

27
00:02:46.741 --> 00:02:59.308
of Kent!" Thunderous applause greeted Edward's speech. "The loyal Earl of Kent will be given property and

28
00:02:59.309 --> 00:03:11.549
gold for his service!" the king went on. Then he turned and pointed at Hugh, who was trying

29
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.382
to retreat from the hall as inconspicuously as he could. "Guards! Seize that man! He is a

30
00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:22.217
murderer, thief, and liar!" The guards quickly obeyed the new king's orders. Miles saw Edith staring at

31
00:03:22.218 --> 00:03:29.200
him, her face full of emotion. "Edith!" Miles ran over to her and kissed her hand. They

32
00:03:29.201 --> 00:03:39.787
both wept. Edward looked on with a satisfied smile. Perhaps someday the two would be free to

33
00:03:39.788 --> 00:03:50.275
marry. While everyone celebrated, Tom stayed in the background, hoping he'd be forgotten. He was greatly relieved

34
00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:56.600
that Edward had come in time to take the throne, but he felt apprehension too. When Edward

35
00:03:56.601 --> 00:04:02.439
had insisted that Tom return to the palace after the coronation, he was sure some terrible punishment awaited

36
00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:09.334
him. "Excuse me, sir," someone called from behind. It was Humphrey. "You don't have to call me

37
00:04:09.335 --> 00:04:17.994
'sir,'" said Tom. "Haven't you heard? I'm not royalty." "You may not be royalty, sir, but you

38
00:04:17.995 --> 00:04:22.816
are surely a person of honor," declared Humphrey. "You have touched the lives of many of us

39
00:04:22.817 --> 00:04:29.919
here at the palace. Some of us remember King Henry's bloody reign and wish that you were

40
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:36.077
still acting as king," he added with feeling. "If his son follows in his footsteps, then—" "Tom

41
00:04:36.078 --> 00:04:39.970
Canty!" Hertford appeared suddenly and stood with his arms crossed. Tom bowed his head and meekly turned

42
00:04:39.971 --> 00:04:50.464
to the man who had, up until just moments ago, been taking orders from him. "The king

43
00:04:50.465 --> 00:04:56.463
wishes to see you," said Hertford. Edward was seated on his throne. He was speaking to Miles, who

44
00:04:56.464 --> 00:05:04.478
was still standing beside Edith. They stopped talking as Tom was led over to the king. Tom

45
00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:08.796
dropped to his knees and pleaded, "Your Majesty, have mercy on me. I meant no harm and

46
00:05:08.797 --> 00:05:19.210
. . ." Edward got up from his throne and stood before Tom. "I owe you thanks,

47
00:05:19.211 --> 00:05:26.868
Tom Canty," said the king. "Thanks? For what, Your Majesty?" Tom asked incredulously. "I have learned the

48
00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:30.936
story of your days from others. I have heard what a merciful and kind ruler you have

49
00:05:30.937 --> 00:05:34.783
been," Edward said. "These are qualities that I lack, but ones that England needs. But I have

50
00:05:34.784 --> 00:05:40.105
learned much," he went on. "I have learned to think of others before myself and to make

51
00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:48.590
sacrifices when necessary. And I have learned from watching the lives of others that many of the laws

52
00:05:48.591 --> 00:05:56.669
in our land are unjust and cruel. I mean to do something about it." "I too have

53
00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:03.256
learned important lessons about remembering others, Your Majesty," Tom said. Then he thought of his mother and

54
00:06:03.257 --> 00:06:14.411
how he had betrayed her. "And . . ." He hung his head again. "I have been

55
00:06:14.412 --> 00:06:20.322
reminded of my love for my family." "As a token of my appreciation, you and your family

56
00:06:20.323 --> 00:06:29.380
will be taken care of for the rest of your lives. You will be given a place

57
00:06:29.381 --> 00:06:37.047
to live. And when you are old enough, you may work in the king's service. There's something

58
00:06:37.048 --> 00:06:45.461
else." Edward said lowering his voice. "I have heard rumors that your father, John Canty, is gone.

59
00:06:45.462 --> 00:06:55.353
He has left London for good." Tom's eyes welled with tears. He bent down to kiss the king's

60
00:06:55.354 --> 00:07:02.535
hand and soon said good-bye. To his surprise his mother and sisters were waiting for him at

61
00:07:02.536 --> 00:07:07.700
the palace gate. "Mother!" Tom cried, as he ran into her outstretched arms. "I'm so sorry!" He

62
00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:14.450
buried his face on her shoulder, deeply ashamed of how he had treated her. "It's all right,

63
00:07:14.451 --> 00:07:20.369
darling boy," his mother said, comforting him. "I understand. Don't say another word." "I will never be

64
00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:28.847
so selfish again," Tom promised. It was a promise he kept for the rest of his days.

65
00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:33.510
King Edward kept his promises too. Soon it was the law that no citizen could die for

66
00:07:33.511 --> 00:07:37.483
a petty crime, and those who faced more serious accusations could not be sentenced without a fair

67
00:07:37.484 --> 00:07:51.751
trial. The king also remembered the many people who'd shown him kindness, including the two women from jail.

68
00:07:51.752 --> 00:08:01.907
He made sure that their daughters had good homes. And for as long as the young king

69
00:08:01.908 --> 00:08:08.303
lived, he remained fond of telling a certain story. It was the story of a prince and

70
00:08:08.304 --> 00:08:19.711
a pauper who, by wearing different clothing, had learned many of the same important lessons about life.

